; DOMAIN: category-theory/enriched [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-26]; DOMAIN: category-theory/enriched [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-26]
; Claim: An end int_c F(c,c) is the universal wedge (terminal object among dinatural transformations from a constant) for F: C^op x C -> D; a coend int^c F(c,c) is the dual cowedge, computable as the coequalizer of the two maps sum_{f:c->c2} F(c2,c) => sum_c F(c,c). Ends generalize limits (int_c Hom(Gc,Fc) = Nat(G,F)) and coends generalize colimits. Yoneda density int^c C(c,-) (x) Fc iso F; co-Yoneda int_c [C(-,c), Fc] iso F; Fubini lets iterated ends/coends commute.
; Structure: (wedge = dinatural cone; end = terminal wedge, coend = initial cowedge) (coend as coequalizer) (end as equalizer dually) (Nat(G,F) = int_c D(Gc,Fc)) (Yoneda density int^c C(c,-)(x)Fc iso F; co-Yoneda int_c [C(-,c),Fc] iso F) (Fubini) (Kan ext as (co)end: Lan_K F(d) = int^c D(Kc,d)(x)Fc, Ran_K F(d) = int_c [D(d,Kc),Fc]) (weighted (co)limit lim^W F = int_c [Wc,Fc], colim^W F = int^c Wc(x)Fc).
; Result: ends/coends are the integral calculus of category theory, packaging limits, colimits, natural transformations, Kan extensions, and weighted (co)limits into one notation where Fubini and Yoneda-density act as computational rules; the natural home for enriched (co)limits.
; Bridge: genesis_yoneda (the density/co-Yoneda formulas are the coend-theoretic strengthening of the Yoneda lemma, and Kan extensions - the categorical shadow of the Ind-Res adjunction in genesis_frobenius_reciprocity - get their pointwise Lan/Ran formula as a coend/end).
